$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for o-Benzenedisulfonimide- Catalyzed Acetalization
(Entry 10, Table 1). To a solution of 4-chlorobenzaldehyde (7a; 0.28 g, 2
mmol) and ethane-1,2-diol (9; 0.37 g, 6 mmol) in toluene (5 mL) was added
o-benzenedisulfonimide (1; 1 mol%; 0.0044 g, 0.02 mmol) and the reaction
mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 60 min. The reaction mixture was treated
with solid NaHCO3, evaporated under reduced pressure, and the residue was
poured into Et2O-H2O (40 mL, 1:1). The aqueous layer was separated. The
organic extract was dried over Na2SO4, and evaporated under reduced
pressure; the crude residue was chromatographed on a short column
(PE-Et2O, 9.5:0.5) with spectral data identical to those reported.19b
4-chlorobenzaldehyde ethlylene acetal (8d), colorless oil, yield 0.32 g,
87%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM o-benzenedisulfonimide: a novel and reusable catalyst for acid-catalyzed
organic reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
