$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure J1: Synthesis of
1-Dimethoxymethyl-4-methylbenzene (1f)2 Methanol (10 mL),
4-methylbenzaldehyde (5f, 2.40 mL, 20.0 mmol), and HC(OMe)3 (3.30 mL,
30.0 mmol) were added to LiBF4 (93.5 mg, 1.00 mmol). The mixture was
stirred and heated to reflux. After 1 h, the reaction mixture was cooled
to r.t. and poured into saturated aqueous NaHCO3. After extraction with
t-BuOMe, the combined organic layer was washed with saturated aqueous
NaCl, dried over Na2SO4, and evaporated. Purification of the residual oil
by distillation. (Dimethoxymethyl)cyclohexane (1h)4 According to
procedure J, 1h (2.74 g, 87% yield, colorless liquid) was obtained by the
reaction using cyclohexanecarbaldehyde (5h, 2.42 mL, 20.0 mmol), HC(OMe)3
(2.84 mL, 26.0 mmol), and LiBF4 (56.3 mg, 0.60 mmol) in MeOH (10 mL) for
3 h.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
