$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Benzaldehyde dibenzyl acetal (Table 2, run 1)
To a mixture of FeCl3 (2.0 mg, 0.012 mmol) and benzaldehyde (61 μl, 0.60
mmol) were added benzyloxytrimethylsilane (284 μl, 1.44 mmol) at 0 °C
under argon atmosphere. The resultant mixture was stirred for 2 h and
quenched with saturated sodium hydrogencarbonate. The organic materials
were extracted with Et2O and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The
solvent was evaporated and benzaldehyde dibenzyl acetal (172.5 mg, 92%)
was isolated by thin-layer chromatography on silica gel (ether : hexane =
1 : 10, including Et3N). The product gave satisfactory 1H and 13C NMR, IR
spectra. yield 87%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron(III) Chloride-Catalyzed Convenient One-Pot Synthesis of Homoallyl
Benzyl Ethers Starting from Aldehydes
