$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of Diethyl Acetals; General
Procedure: To a mixture of carbonyl compound 1 (5 mmol) and
(EtO)3CH(10-12.5 mmol), WCl6 (0.05-0.1 mmol) was added, and the resulting
solution was stirred at room temperature and the progress of the reaction
was monitored by TLC or GC After completion of the reaction (Table 1), a
cooled aqueous solution or NaOH (10%,25 mL) was added and the mixture was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 25 mL). The organic extracts was washed with
water (2 x25 mL) and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Evaporation of the
solvent under reduced pressure gave almost pure product(s). Further
purification was proceeded by vacuum distillation to afford pure diethyl
acetal 2 in good to excellent yield (Table 1). 2f, yield 87 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tungsten hexachloride (WCl6), a highly efficient and chemoselective
catalyst for acetalization of carbonyl compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Firouzabadi, H.; Iranpoor, N.; Karimi, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1999), 29(13), 2255-2263

