$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of D-mannitol (5.0 g, 27 mmol), ciclohexanone (8.4 mL, 81
mmol), triethyl orthoformate (4.5 mL, 27 mmol), BF3·Et2O (0.3 mL, 2.7
mmol) and dry DMSO (11 mL) was stirred for 13 h at rt. The mixture was
then poured into 20 mL of 10% ice-cooled NaHCO3 solution and was
extracted with ether (15 mL × 3). The organic layer was dried over MgSO4
and concentrated in vacuo. To a solution of the residue obtained in 100
mL of ether was added a solution of NaIO4 (7.3 g, 34 mmol) and Bu4NF
(0.22 mL, 0.7 mmol) in 60 mL of water, and the mixture was stirred for 4
h at rt. The mixture was separated and aqueous layer was extracted with
ether (15 mL × 3). The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. 8.6 g (87%) of
2,3-O-cyclohexylidene-D-glyceraldehyde as an oil.
