$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Reductive Aldol Reaction Using GeCl2-dioxane with
MeOH quenching. To a stirred suspension of Bu4NBr (0.006 mmol),
GeCl2-dioxanecomplex (0.6 mmol) and aldehyde 2 (0.6 mmol) in solvent (2
mL) was added bromoaldehyde 1(0.6 mmol) under nitrogen. The reaction
mixture was stirred under the reaction conditions noted in the text.
Methanol (8 mL) was added and the resulting solution was stirred for
additional 1 h at room temperature. Then aqueous NaHCO3 (saturated; 5 mL)
was added to the reaction mixture. The resulting mixture was extracted
with Et2O/hexane (4/1), and organic layer was dried over
MgSO4.{PARA]product, yield 86%. Information not present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reductive cross-aldol reaction using bromo aldehyde and an aldehyde
mediated by germanium(II): One-pot, large-scale protocol
