$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (7) General Procedure for the preparation of
diethyl acetals.-Method A: To a solution of carbonyl compound 1 (5 mmol),
(EtO)3CH (7.5-15 mmol), absolute ethanol (25 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (25 mL), NBS
(0.05-0.25 mmol) was added and the resulting solution was stirred at room
temperature. After completion of the reaction (TLC or GC), a cold aqueous
solution of NaOH (10%, 25 mL) was added and the mixture was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (3 × 40 mL). The organic extracts were washed with water (2 ×
20 mL) and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Evaporation of the solvent under
reduced pressure gave almost pure product(s). Further purification was
proceeded by vacuum distillation to afford pure diethyl acetals 2 in good
to excellent yields (Table). Table Acelalization of Carbonyl Compounds
with (EtO)3CH and NBS under Almost Neutral Reaction Conditions Entry 3
Table Acelalization of Carbonyl Compounds with (EtO)3CH and NBS under
Almost Neutral Reaction Conditions Entry 7 Yield 85%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
