$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Reductive Aldol Reaction
Using GeCl2-dioxane with MeOH quenching. To a stirred suspension of
Bu4NBr (0.006 mmol), GeCl2-dioxanecomplex (0.6 mmol) and aldehyde 2 (0.6
mmol) in solvent (2 mL) was added bromoaldehyde 1(0.6 mmol) under
nitrogen. The reaction mixture was stirred under the reaction conditions
noted in the text. Methanol (8 mL) was added and the resulting solution
was stirred for additional 1 h at room temperature. Then aqueous NaHCO3
(saturated; 5 mL) was added to the reaction mixture. The resulting
mixture was extracted with Et2O/hexane (4/1), and organic layer was dried
over MgSO4.{PARA]product, yield 86%.
(1R*,2R*)-2-Dimethoxymethyl-3-methyl-1-phenyl-1-butanol (syn-4ba)., 85%.
IR: (neat) 3467 (OH) cm-1; 1H NMR: (270 MHz, CDCl3) 7.37-7.19 (m, 5H,
Ar), 5.29 (brs, 1H, 1-H), 4.43 (d, J = 3.4 Hz, 1H, 2-CHOMe)2), 3.49 (s,
3H, OMeA), 3.43 (s, 3H, OMeB), 3.29 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H, OH, DJO
exchangeable), 2.01-1.89 (m, 1H, 3-H), 1.83 (ddd, J = 3.3, 3.3, 3.3 Hz,
1H, 2-H), 1.00 (d, J = 7.1Hz, 3H, 3-CH3), 0.77 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H, 4-H3);
1H NMR: (270 MHz, CDCl3, small amount of D2O) 7.37-7.19 (m, 5H, Ar), 5.29
(d, J = 2.4 Hz 1H, 1-H), 4.43 (d, J = 3.4 Hz, 1H, 2-CH(OMe)2), 3.49 (s,
3H, OMeA), 3.43 (s, 3H, OMeB), 2.01-1.89 (m, 1H, 3-H), 1.83 (ddd, J =
3.5, 3.5, 3.5 Hz,1H, 2-H), 1.00 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H, 3-CH3), 0.77 (d, J =
7.1 Hz, 3H, 4-H3); 13C NMR: (67.9 MHz,CDCl3) 143.80 (s, i-Ph), 127.75 (d,
m-Ph), 126.26 (d, p-Ph), 125.66 (d, o-Ph), 107.03 (d, 2-CH(OMe)2), 72.11
(d, C-1), 55.57 (q, OMeA), 54.99 (q, OMeB), 52.25 (d, C-2), 24.33 (d,
C-3),23.11 (q, C-4), 20.53 (q, 3-CH3); MS: (CI, 70 eV) m/z 121
(PhCH(OH)CH + 1, 15), 107(PhCHOH, 25), 101 ((CH3)2CHCHCHOMe + 1, 100), 75
(CH(OMe)2, 28). Anal. Calcd for C14H22O3 (238.32): C, 70.56; H, 9.30.
Found C, 70.49; H, 8.87.
