$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 1: Acetal Formation: To a
stirred substituted 2-bromobenzadehyde (1.0 equiv.) in toluene (50 mL),
1,3-propanediol (1.5 equiv.) and p-toluene sulphonic acid (PTSA) (0.1
equiv.) were added and the solution was heated at reflux under Dean-Stark
conditions for 3 hours. After cooling to room temperature, the reaction
mixture was washed with water, the organic extract dried using MgSO4 and
the solvent evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude compounds were
purified by recrystallisation using a suitable solvent system. From
2-bromobenzadehyde (10.0 g, 54 mmol), 1,3-propanediol (6.16 g, 81 mmol)
and PTSA (0.86 g, 5 mmol). The crude was purified by recrystallisation
from diethyl ether. From 2-bromo-4-methylbenzaldehyde 0.56 g, 2.8 mmol),
1,3-propanediol (0.30 mL, 4.2 mmol) and PTSA (0.05 g, 0.2 mmol). The
crude was purified by recrystallisation from diethyl ether.
2-(2-Bromo-4-methylphenyl)-1,3-dioxane, a pale yellow oil, yield 0.61 g,
85%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δH = 7.47 (1H, d, J = 8.0 Hz, CBrCH), 7.26
(1H, d, J = 1.0 Hz, Ar), 7.04 (1H, d, J = 8.0 Hz, Ar), 5.63 (1H, s,
ArCH), 4.18-4.10 (2H, app. ddd, J = 12.0, 5.0 and 1.0 Hz, OCH2),
3.95-3.85 (2H, m, OCH2), 2.21 (3H, s, ArCH3), 2.18-2.04 (1H, m, OCH2CH2),
1.32 (1H, app. d of septet, J = 13.5 and 1.5, OCH2CH2); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δC = 140.6, 134.7, 133.0, 128.3, 127.8, 122.1, 101.0, 67.6, 25.7,
20.9; IR (film / cm-1) ν = 2851 (O-CH-O); HRMS: m/z (ES) 279.0002,
C11H13O2Br [M+Na]+ requires 278.9997.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark conditions used
