$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure Bromoaldehyde 1(0.6 mmol)
was added to a stirred solution of 3(0.6 mmol) and aldehyde 2(0.6 mmol)
in THF (2 mL) at 0 °C. After the mixture was stirred for 4-12 h at 0 °C,
MeOH (8 mL) was added and the resulting solution was stirred for
additional 1 h at r.t. Then, aq NaHCO3 (sat., 10 mL) was added. The
mixture was extracted with Et2O- hexane (4:1, three times) and the
organic layer was dried over MgSO4 . The solvent was evaporated under
reduced pressure and the residue was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel to give the product Compound 4ad, yield 85%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Germanium(II)-mediated reductive cross-aldol reaction of aldehydes:
synthesis of aldols with diastereocontrolled quaternary carbon centers
