$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedures:17
4-(2,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)-2,2-diethyl-1,3-dioxolane (7a). p-Toluenesulfonic
acid (ca. 25 mg) was added to a solution of 3-pentanone (4a, 950 mg, 11
mmol), (2,5-dimethoxyphenyl)ethylene glycol (6, 2 g, 10 mmol), and
triethyl orthoformate (1.8 mL, 1.62 g, 11 mmol) in dichloromethane (10
mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight and
then purified by chromatography. A 2.05 g sample of acetal 7a was
obtained as colorless liquid.
4-(2,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)-2-phenyl-1,3-dioxolane (7b, 1:1 mixture of
diastereomers): Colorless liquid, 85%. 1H NMR: δ 3.69-3.87 (4s, 12H + 2t,
2H), 4.46 (t, 1H), 4.67 (t, 1H), 5.47 (2t, 2H), 5.98 (s, 1H), 6.08 (s,
1H), 6.79 (m, 4H), 7.12 (m, 1H), 7.19 (m, 1H), 7.40 – 7.54 (m, 5H), 7.55
– 7.59 (m, 5H). MS: 286 (100, M+), 227 (11), 180 (48), 164 (17), 149
(40), 119 (44), 105 (39), 91 (74), 89 (16), 77 (53). HRMS: calcd. for
C17H18O4Na+ 309.1103; found 309.1115
