$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method for preparation of tetrahydropyran
derivatives. A mixture of 3-butene-1-ol (4 mmol), 4-chlorobenzalehyde (2
mmol) and PANI-TsOH (0.25 mmol) or PANI-FeCl3 (0.25 mmol) in
dichloromethane (10 ml) was refluxed for the specified reaction period.
On completion, as indicated by TLC, the catalyst was filtered and washed
with dichloromethane (2 ×15 ml). The combined organic layers were washed
with water, sodium bicarbonate solution, dried over anhydrous sodium
sulfate and concentrated in vacuum. The resulting reaction mass was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (Merck,60-120 mesh) using
hexane and ethyl acetate as eluent to afford 2,4 disubstituted
tetrahydropyran ether as pure product. Di-(3-butenoxy)methyl-3
nitrobenzaldehyde (7e, new compound): Colourless liquid, yield 84%. 1HNMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.33(s, 1H), 8.15(d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.80(d, J =
7.7Hz, 1H), 7.53 (t, J = 7.7Hz,1H), 5.81-5.82(m,2H), 5.60(s, 1H),
5.07-5.12(m, 4H), 3.55- 3.56(m,4H), 2.38(q, J = 6.7Hz, 4H); IR(KBr)cm-1
2921, 1704, 1642, 1530, 1473, 1436, 1350, 1206, 1111, 1051, 990, 916;13C
NMR(CDCl3, 400 MHz,ppm): δ = 147.9, 140.6, 134.6, 132.6, 128.9, 123.0,
121.7, 116.5, 99.6, 64.5, 34.3; GC/MS: m/z (%base peak) (M+ )277, 222,
206, 205, 176, 153, 152, 136, 121, 105, 77, 57, 55(100); CHN Anal. Cal
C15H19O4 N; C 64.70, H 6.86, N 5.07; found C 64.90, H 6.85, N 5.05.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, solid-supported catalyst, polyaniline-supported
TsOH prepared and used as catalyst, catalyst recyclable, mechanism
studied, alternatively polyaniline-supported FeCl3 used as catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Investigation of Prins reaction for the synthesis of 2,4-disubstituted
tetrahydropyran derivatives and 1,3-dioxanes using polyaniline supported
acid as reusable catalyst
