$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure of
a-Halogenation and Acetalization Piperidine (2.5 mmol) and 4A molecular
sieves (15 g) were added into a mixture of substrate (10 mmol),
DCDMH/DBDMH (20 mmol), and methanol (35mL). After reflux for 12 h (or
heating to 50-52 °C when DBDMH was used), the mixture was filtered, and
the solvent of methanol was removed from the filtrate under reduced
press. After MTBE (50 mL) was added to the residue, the organic layer was
washed by water (40mL) and brine (50 mL) several times, and the organic
layer was dried on Na2SO4. After that, the organic layer was filtered,
and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The product was
obtained. 1-(2-Chloro-1,1-dimethoxyethyl)-4-nitrobenzene (2a)
1-(2-Bromo-1,1-dimethoxyethyl)-2,4-dichlorobenzene (3g) Light yellow oil.
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ: 7.78 (d, 1H, J=8.5 Hz, Ar-H), 7.39 (s, 1H,
Ar-H), 7.27 (d, 1H, J=8.5 Hz, Ar-H), 3.88 (s, 2H, -CH2), 3.21 (s, 6H,
-OCH3).[12]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieve used, reagent (molecular sieve) recyclable, mechanism
studied
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Step Conversion of Acetophenones to α-Haloacetophenone Dimethyl
Acetals Using DCDMH/DBDMH and Molecular Sieve in Methanol
